Replace the deprecated Qt calls of the Qt 5 style

Qt 5.15 marks calls of the Qt 5 tree as deprecated, and the style build
prints a warning line for most of them. Each call now uses the API that
Qt 5.15 offers.

QPalette::Background, QPalette::Foreground, QStyle::PE_FrameStatusBar and
QStyle::PE_IndicatorViewItemCheck are aliases. They become
QPalette::Window, QPalette::WindowText, PE_FrameStatusBarItem and
PE_IndicatorItemViewItemCheck, and the values stay the same.

QString::SkipEmptyParts becomes Qt::SkipEmptyParts, and both enumerators
hold the value 1. QWheelEvent::pos() becomes position().toPoint(), the
expression that the header holds. QLayout::setMargin(n) becomes
setContentsMargins(n, n, n, n). QApplication::globalStrut() has no
replacement, and the call goes, because the default strut is 0 by 0.

Qt offers no other name for PM_DefaultTopLevelMargin,
PM_DefaultChildMargin and PM_DefaultLayoutSpacing, so the three cases go.
The PM_Layout*Margin case now holds the values: 9 pixels for a window, 2
for OpenOffice with no widget, and 6 for any other widget.

layoutSpacing() returns 6 pixels. Qt reads the PM_Layout* metrics and
layoutSpacing() for a layout, so the layouts keep their margins and gaps.
A direct caller now gets the QCommonStyle values: 11, 9 and 6 pixels at
96 dots per inch, not 9, 6 and 6. QCommonStyle grows the three with the
screen resolution, and the configuration dialog now sets 6 pixels itself.

Qt::SkipEmptyParts and QWheelEvent::position() need Qt 5.14, so
QT_MIN_VERSION rises from 5.3.2 to 5.14 and find_package() carries it.
Qt 5.15 is the last Qt 5 release.

The change sits on the branch work/qt6-deprecated-api of the local tree. The
fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !11 on system/qtcurve holds
that branch as the source.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

